&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Braze, we have found our people. We’re a genuinely approachable, exceptionally kind, and intensely passionate crew.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek to ignite that passion by setting high standards, championing teamwork, and creating work-life harmony as we collectively navigate rapid growth on a global scale while striving for greater equity and opportunity – inside and outside our organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To flourish here, you must be prepared to set a high bar for yourself and those around you. There is always a way to contribute: Acting with autonomy, having accountability and being open to new perspectives are essential to our continued success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our deep curiosity to learn and our eagerness to share diverse passions with others gives us balance and injects a one-of-a-kind vibrancy into our culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are driven to solve exhilarating challenges and have a bias toward action in the face of change, you will be empowered to make a real impact here, with a sharp and passionate team at your back. If Braze sounds like a place where you can thrive, we can’t wait to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Core data objects are at the base of Braze&#39;s product offering and power our industry-leading customer engagement tool. The Core Objects team owns our customers&#39; most valuable data structures — the foundation that enables them to use Braze most effectively and implement their most innovative strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team extensively integrates AI into its daily workflow, leveraging agentic tools to navigate our large Ruby monolith, create proof of concepts, and transition quickly and safely from an ask to a working solution. AI has been used across all stages of product delivery, fundamentally enhancing the team’s ability to deliver high-quality results more efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Staff Fullstack Engineer to join the Core Objects team as a hands-on technical leader. You will create and own complex systems end to end, from the data model and the ingestion path through the APIs and the dashboard experience customers use every day, at the scale demanded by some of the biggest brands in the world. You will help decide what gets built, not only how. Architecture, performance, and cost are constant considerations, but your success will be measured by the value you unlock for customers. Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect &amp;amp; Build: conceive, design, and implement large-scale systems and services that handle massive data volumes and complex workloads in real time, including extending our high-scale ingestion pipeline to ingest new and advanced data objects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Product: partner with product to define what gets built and why, then keep improving it after launch as you learn how customers actually use it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Core Systems: take ownership of the complex backend systems behind Braze&#39;s core data objects, continuously improving their performance, reliability, and cost-effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor &amp;amp; Influence: lead by example and mentor engineers on best practices in software design, coding, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate Cross-Functionally: work closely with other engineering teams, product managers, and stakeholders to ensure core data systems are effectively integrated and aligned with business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovate &amp;amp; Optimize: continuously identify opportunities to improve our systems, research new technologies, and advocate for their adoption where appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain &amp;amp; Evolve: support and refine operational procedures (alerts, on-call rotation, troubleshooting playbooks) to maximize system stability and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO YOU ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive Software Engineering Experience: 7+ years of professional experience, including hands-on work in full-stack development or back-end services, particularly with high-scale, high-throughput systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product Ownership at Scale: proven track record of delivering customer-facing products on high-scale data systems, from problem definition through launch and adoption. You can point to what customers or the business gained, not only what the system did&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems at Scale: proven track record of building foundational data-driven systems at scale - whether streaming, real-time pipelines, or large-scale data platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Leadership: skilled at driving architectural direction, scoping large efforts, and effectively managing technical debt. Known for precise communication of complex technical concepts and a willingness to drive major technical initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Fundamentals: deep understanding of software design, data structures, and algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-Starter: great communication and organizational skills, with a history of thriving in team environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Languages/Frameworks: familiarity with Ruby, Ruby on Rails, React, Go, and SQL/NoSQL databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Database Experience: previous experience with MongoDB, Snowflake, or other data lake solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud Technologies: experience with container orchestration (Kubernetes), and cloud services (AWS, GCP, Azure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architecture: experience with distributed systems, API design, monitoring, and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For candidates based in Canada, the pay range at the start of employment for this position is expected to be between CA$ 220,000 and CA$ 359,213/year, with an expected On Target Earnings (OTE) between CA$ 244,000.00 and CA$ 298,400/year (including performance-based or variable compensation (bonus or commission). Your particular offer may vary depending on multiple individual factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. In addition to cash compensation, this role qualifies for a comprehensive Total Rewards package that includes equity grants of restricted stock (RSUs) so that you will own a piece of our company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Braze benefits vary by location, and we encourage you to review our specific benefits offerings for each country &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.braze.com/company/careers/how-we-hire#benefit-section&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;. More details on benefits plans will be provided if you receive an offer of employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From offering comprehensive benefits to fostering hybrid ways of working, we’ve got you covered so you can prioritize work-life harmony. Braze offers benefits such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation that may include equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement and Employee Stock Purchase Plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive benefit plans covering medical, dental, vision, life, and disability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family services that include fertility benefits and equal paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development supported by formal career pathing, learning platforms, and a yearly learning stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A curated in-office employee experience, designed to foster community, team connections, and innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to give back to your community, including an annual company-wide Volunteer Week and donation matching&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Resource Groups that provide supportive communities within Braze&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, transparent, and fun culture recognized as a Great Place to Work®&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT BRAZE&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Braze is the leading customer engagement platform that empowers brands to Be Absolutely Engaging™. Braze helps brands deliver great customer experiences that drive value both for consumers and for their businesses. Built on a foundation of composable intelligence, BrazeAI™ allows marketers to combine and activate AI agents, models, and features at every touchpoint throughout the Braze Customer Engagement Platform for smarter, faster, and more meaningful customer engagement. From cross-channel messaging and journey orchestration to Al-powered decisioning and optimization, Braze enables companies to turn action into interaction through autonomous, 1:1 personalized experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company has been consistently recognized as a Leader in marketing technology by industry analysts, and was named a G2 “Best of Marketing and Digital Advertising Software Product” in 2026. Braze was also named a 2026 Best Places to Work by Built In, a 2025 America’s Greenest Companies by Newsweek, and a 2025 Fortune Best Workplace in Technology™ by Great Place To Work®. Braze is also proudly certified as a Great Place to Work® in the U.S., the UK, Australia, and Singapore.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company is headquartered in New York with offices in Austin, Berlin, Bucharest, Chicago, Dubai, Jakarta, London, Paris, San Francisco, São Paulo, Singapore, Seoul, Sydney and Tokyo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;BRAZE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Braze, we strive to create equitable growth and opportunities inside and outside the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
